            "review_title": "Review at Oopen Restaurant - Ibis Saigon South",
            "review_text": "Christopher D\nHo Chi Minh City, null, Vietnam\n6 contributions\n0\nGood Food. SLOW service.\nApr 2014 • Family\nBeen here a few times because we're in the area. The food is pretty good and the prices are decent. However, the service is the SLOWEST I have experienced... and that says a lot. It hasn't been busy any of the times we were here, but getting a club sandwich, a burger, and a bowl of noodles took over 30 minutes. But we came back thinking it was just a bad day. Stopped in for lunch (only 3 other tables of customers), ordered a bowl of noodles, an omelette, and a bowl of pasta. After 30 minutes we got up and left because the waitstaff said it would be \"just a few more minutes\" (they had said the same thing about 10 minutes earlier too). If you're not planning to go anywhere and want to sit around having a few drinks it might work, but otherwise the wait is too long to recommend.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 30, 2014",
