            "review_title": "Review at Oopen Restaurant - Ibis Saigon South",
            "review_text": "vietnamnomad\nHo Chi Minh City\n7 contributions\n0\nA really good meal in Phu My Hung\nSep 2012 • Friends\nI always believed that you couldn't find good food in a hotel restaurant, but lunch at the \"OOPEN Restaurant\" proved me wrong today. \nFirst of all the drinks, cocktails, mocktails... are the most original and best tasting I've had in Vietnam. (And I've been coming here since 1994!) And the food is incredibly good and reasonably priced. I was in the mood for a juicy cheeseburger as a change from my daily spring roll, and my Vietnamese friend wanted to have some french food! Well not only was the food scrumptious but the service was friendly, kind, efficient, and everyone spoke english. A nice way to spend an afternoon over a quiet lunch with your friend.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten September 11, 2012\nTchang_LEE_ISS\nDear Guest,\n\nGreetings from ibis Saigon South!\n\nOn behalf of the management and staff of ibis Saigon South, we would like to thank you for using our Oopen restaurant. Especially, we would like to deeply thank you for your comments about our Oopen restaurant's food and staff service.\n\nYour comments have certainly motivated our team members to further develop our service of staff for the benefit of valuable guests, such as yourself. And it will give us more reason to do our best to be professional, efficient and friendly. \n\nAgain, thank you for choosing ibis Saigon South. And, we would like to welcome you in the future.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nTchang Young Lee\nGeneral Manager\nibis Saigon South\nRead more\nWritten September 14, 2012\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
